 who is the villain  villain you know you Tony kind of serves  as the primary antagonist really but the  actual mustache holy bad guy is Zemo and  he's like many Marvel villains he's kind  of forgettable but I will say I really  like the way that they motivated him  which is that it's just simple basic  revenge very personal they didn't try  and make it big it's not some big global  scheme he's not part of Hydra you know  wheels turning within wheels got to take  over the world no he just wants to tear  apart this team cuz he blames them for  his law  and given how much characters personal  drives and personal motivations are  driving really the entire narrative in  the entire conflict having the villain  be driven by the same kind of thing was  a really smart decision so he functions  very well but just it is not  particularly memorable but that Manny  was never gonna be because the  interesting conflict is between Tony and  Steve and the one other complaint I'm  gonna make is and this is actually sort  of a praise by exception because you  know I singled out some characters I'm  not gonna single out every single  character because the characters are all  great everybody gets a wonderful  highlighted moment everybody gets you  know a bit where we really get you know  some really fun moments with the  character that you really feel why it  was important that they were around  except for Rhodey  except for Warmachine because unlike  every other character he's the only one  who just feels like hanger-on he's there  because Tony's there and really no other  reason I mean with Sam Wilson the Falcon  they made him feel like he has his own  agency Rudy  wrote he's just kind of their the  franchise's never really figured out  what to do with him ever since they gave  him the war machine armor and when he  gets clipped by vision and crashes that  felt kind of forced I was like okay okay  I mean it didn't it doesn't derail the  movie and it's actually a very large  praise of